---
import BaseLayout from '../shared/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Prompt from '../shared/ui/Prompt.astro';
import { profile } from '../features/seo/seo';
---

<BaseLayout title={`Privacy Policy | ${profile.contact.name}`} description="Privacy policy for the site and messaging interactions." currentPage="/privacy-policy">
  <Prompt command="cat privacy-policy.md" />
  <div class="output">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 28 Oct 2026</p>

      <p>Welcome to www.amrithnath.dev (&quot;we,&quot; &quot;our,&quot; or &quot;us&quot;). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you visit the website or contact the business through WhatsApp. By accessing or using the website or engaging with us on WhatsApp, you agree to this Privacy Policy.</p>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect personal information that you voluntarily provide, such as your name, email address, phone number, and any other details you submit through contact forms, WhatsApp messages, or newsletter sign-ups. We may also collect non-personal information such as browser type, IP address, and pages visited to improve the website's functionality.</p>

      <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Respond to inquiries and provide support via website forms and WhatsApp messages.</li>
        <li>Improve and personalize the website and WhatsApp communication experience.</li>
        <li>Send newsletters, updates, or promotional content if you have opted in.</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing of Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information. We may share information with service providers who assist in website operations and WhatsApp Business services, comply with legal obligations, or protect our rights.</p>

      <h2>WhatsApp Business Data Privacy</h2>
      <p>When you contact us through WhatsApp, we may collect your phone number, profile information, and message content. This information is used solely to respond to your inquiries, provide support, and improve our services.</p>
      <p>WhatsApp is a third-party platform, and your data may also be subject to WhatsApp's own privacy policy. Review <a href="https://www.whatsapp.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">WhatsApp's Privacy Policy</a> for more details.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
      <p>This website does not set cookies. It stores your theme preference in your browser's local storage, which never leaves your device.</p>
      <p>Page views are counted with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which is cookieless and does not fingerprint or track you across sites. It records aggregate data only: the page visited, referrer, country, and browser and device type. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, the analytics script is not loaded at all. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>

      <p>Site search runs in your browser using a same-origin, build-time index. The search page does not load analytics or send queries to an external search service. Shared search URLs include the query, so it may appear in browser history and site access logs.</p>
      <h3>Article view counts</h3>
      <p>Blog posts and project pages may show a public view count. It is a single anonymous number per page, kept by a small service at <code>views.amrithnath.dev</code> on Cloudflare. When you open an article, your browser asks that service for the count and, the first time you view that article, adds one to it. The service stores only the page path and its total. It does not set cookies and does not store your IP address, browser details, or any identifier, so views cannot be linked to you or to each other.</p>
      <p>To avoid counting you twice, your browser remembers in local storage which articles it has already counted; this never leaves your device, and you can clear it at any time. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, the count is only displayed and never increased.</p>

      <h3>Carbon badge</h3>
      <p>The footer shows an estimate of the page's carbon footprint. On this site, your browser asks the Website Carbon API (<code>api.websitecarbon.com</code>, run by Wholegrain Digital) for the result for the page address you are viewing, without cookies or a referrer, and caches the answer in local storage for a day. As with any web request, that service receives your IP address. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal, no request is made; in that case, or if the service is unavailable, the estimate is calculated entirely in your browser from the page's own size.</p>
      <p>On wide screens the side panel also shows live page performance and a carbon estimate calculated in your browser; that data never leaves your device apart from a running byte total kept in session storage.</p>

      <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>The website may contain links to third-party sites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of these external sites, and we encourage you to review their privacy policies before providing personal information.</p>

      <h2>Data Security</h2>
      <p>We implement security measures to protect your information. However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to access, correct, or delete your personal information. To exercise these rights, contact <a href="mailto:amrithnathvijayakumar@gmail.com">amrithnathvijayakumar@gmail.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
